{
  "comment": "Shared accept/reject fixtures for rc2fx-core. The Go port (desktop/core, shared_fixtures_test.go) and the Rust crate (crates/rc2fx-core/tests/shared_fixtures.rs) read the same files; each checks its own direction. For accepted cases the decoded value, written back, must equal `canonical` (compact) and `pretty` (to_string_pretty) byte for byte. The Go port reaches every verdict; the Rust crate skips the reject cases of documents only the desktop reads (deviceState, deviceVersions, sshStatus, meter, diagnosticsEvents, presetSummaries). A rejected case with `error` must fail with exactly that message on each side that reads it. generate.py writes this directory: change it and run it rather than editing files by hand. .gitattributes keeps every byte as committed (CRLF and odd bytes are part of some cases).",
